<ProgramDetailPage
  title="Post-Graduation Work Permit (PGWP) | Entrypoint Canada"
  description="Learn how your school, study program, status, and graduation timing can affect your Canadian post-graduation work permit (PGWP) application."
  kicker="Student Pathways"
  heading="Post-Graduation Work Permit (PGWP)"
  summary="A post-graduation work permit can help eligible international graduates gain Canadian work experience after completing a qualifying program. PGWP rules are detailed and change over time, so study choices and application timing should be reviewed carefully."
  badges={[
    'Canada.ca PGWP source reviewed',
    'Relevant for international students and graduates',
    'Study program and school details matter',
    'Canadian work experience may support later PR planning',
  ]}
  sections={[
    {
      title: 'What a PGWP is',
      body: 'A post-graduation work permit is an open work permit that may be available to eligible graduates of certain Canadian study programs. It can allow a graduate to work in Canada after completing studies, subject to current IRCC requirements.',
      bullets: [
        'The school and program must meet current PGWP requirements',
        'The length and type of study can affect the work permit outcome',
        'Timing after graduation is important for application planning',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Who should review this pathway',
      body: 'Students considering Canada, current international students, and recent graduates should review PGWP eligibility before assuming a program will support future work or permanent residence goals. A study plan should be assessed before enrollment where possible.',
      bullets: [
        'Prospective students comparing programs and schools',
        'Students approaching graduation or permit expiry',
        'Graduates planning Canadian work experience for Express Entry or other pathways',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Common planning issues',
      body: 'PGWP planning is not only about filing a work permit application. It can include reviewing study permit conditions, school status, program length, transcripts, completion letters, passport validity, timing, and whether later permanent residence routes may be realistic.',
      bullets: [
        'Study permit compliance and status history',
        'Graduation documents and application timing',
        'Work experience strategy after the PGWP is issued',
      ],
    },
  ]}
  noteTitle="Student pathway note"
  noteBody="PGWP eligibility depends on current IRCC rules, the designated learning institution, the study program, length of study, and the applicant's circumstances. A consultation can help identify issues before an application is submitted."
  sourceLinks={[
    { label: 'Canada.ca PGWP page', href: 'https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/work/after-graduation.html' },
    { label: 'Canada.ca study permit page', href: 'https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit.html' },
  ]}
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Programs overview', href: '/programs/' },
    { label: 'Study and work permit services', href: '/services/#work-study' },
    { label: 'Book a consultation', href: '/contact/' },
